# Local tooling config, not part of the project
.claude/

# Godot 4+ ignores
.godot/
/android/
*.translation

# Build output — regenerate with tools/build.sh
build/

# EOS native binaries — ~240 MB of prebuilt libraries plus Epic's own SDK.
#
# The GDScript half of the addon IS committed; only bin/ is ignored, because a
# quarter of a gigabyte of platform binaries bloats the repo permanently and git
# cannot forget them afterwards. Restore on a fresh clone, and in CI before any
# export, with:
#
#   tools/fetch-eos.sh
#
# Git LFS is the alternative, but it spends bandwidth quota on every clone for
# files that are already published, versioned and immutable upstream.
addons/epic-online-services-godot/bin/

# A folder of screenshots that ended up inside the project. Godot imports
# anything under the project root, so these acquired .import files and started
# looking like assets — 2.7 GB of them. Ignored rather than deleted: they are
# not the project's to throw away.
scripts/Documents/

# export_presets.cfg is deliberately NOT ignored. Godot's default template
# excludes it because it can hold signing keys and passwords; ours holds
# neither, and it carries the include_filter that puts the word lists in the
# build. Without it committed, a fresh clone exports a game with no dictionary.
